<title>SPAIN: La Caixa says lifts Repsol stake to 5.3 pct.</title>
<headline>La Caixa says lifts Repsol stake to 5.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Catalan savings bank La Caixa has bought a 0.3 percent stake in energy group Repsol, lifting its total participation to 5.3 percent, a spokesman for the bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The stake increase cost La Caixa 3.8 billion pesetas on the stock market, at a average price per share of 4,070 pesetas.</p>
<p>La Caixa now becomes the third largest shareholder of the oil group, after state holding firm SEPI and Banco Bilbao Vizcaya which has around 7 percent of Repsol.</p>
<p>The government is to sell its 10 percent Repsol stake in early 1997.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
